<title>USA: CBOT options membership trades at record $175,000.</title>
<headline>CBOT options membership trades at record $175,000.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Board of Trade said a commodity options membership (COM) changed hands at a record $175,000 on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The previous record for a COM, which allows trading of all CBOT options contracts, was $160,000 set on March 12.</p>
<p>The bid and ask prices for a COM were now at $165,000 and $210,000 respectively, the exchange added.</p>
<p>((Chicago Derivatives Desk 312-408-8750))</p>
<p>E-mail: derivatives@reuters.com</p>
